#: ../../source/docs/common-non-gps-navigation-landing-page.rst:7
#: c99da240951e420a81793d320f357b86
msgid "Non-GPS Navigation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-non-gps-navigation-landing-page.rst:12
#: 335d9a5429d34d58858df4e48dfd8d51
msgid "These are the available options that allow a vehicle to estimate its position without a GPS.  Once enabled this allows all autonomous and semi-autonomous modes just as they do would a GPS is available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-non-gps-navigation-landing-page.rst:14
#: 53ccd387879f4258923ba7ab801ca4b4
msgid "unless added via a custom build (see :ref:`common-custom-firmware`), Beacon functionality is not included in standard firmware for autopilots having less than 2MB of flash."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-non-gps-navigation-landing-page.rst:27
#: d526cd578ae147758f7ffe4f44b96a32
msgid "Most of the above systems (except Beacons) require that the ORIGIN be set manually, except if a GPS is present. In order to do this the user must either use the GCS to set Origin, as shown below using Mission Planner, or use a lua script like this `one <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_Scripting/applets/ahrs-set-origin.lua>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-non-gps-navigation-landing-page.rst:32
#: 66a7ec51481e4506a502b0bccd92c83b
msgid "Persistent Origin Storage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-non-gps-navigation-landing-page.rst:34
#: a44094423a4f4bbca9f80a44e1460f8b
msgid "In ArduPilot 4.7 and later, the EKF origin can be automatically saved and restored across power cycles using the following parameters:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-non-gps-navigation-landing-page.rst:36
#: b554a300e55f4b97b8aa8a1892a6dbfd
msgid ":ref:`AHRS_OPTIONS<AHRS_OPTIONS>` bit 3 (RecordOrigin): When enabled, the current EKF origin is automatically saved to parameters whenever it becomes valid (e.g. after GPS lock or manual origin set). The saved origin is stored in:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-non-gps-navigation-landing-page.rst:38
#: 1b429e4a953747f98958780499c7ca24
msgid ":ref:`AHRS_ORIGIN_LAT<AHRS_ORIGIN_LAT>` - Last known origin latitude (degrees)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-non-gps-navigation-landing-page.rst:39
#: 84f131f651724fa68ef0f6693736ee70
msgid ":ref:`AHRS_ORIGIN_LON<AHRS_ORIGIN_LON>` - Last known origin longitude (degrees)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-non-gps-navigation-landing-page.rst:40
#: 82002be5c4424954b7399961ce36d1e2
msgid ":ref:`AHRS_ORIGIN_ALT<AHRS_ORIGIN_ALT>` - Last known origin altitude (meters)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-non-gps-navigation-landing-page.rst:42
#: 19e66ce1ac0a494ca7885b6f0ec2d64a
msgid ":ref:`AHRS_OPTIONS<AHRS_OPTIONS>` bit 4 (UseRecordedOriginForNonGPS): When enabled, the AHRS will automatically restore the saved origin on boot when GPS is not being used. This allows position-controlled flight modes (Loiter, Auto, Guided, etc.) to work indoors without GPS after the origin has been recorded from a previous flight."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-non-gps-navigation-landing-page.rst:44
#: 944793a4f7684500bf925cc3cbc2bae0
msgid "This eliminates the need to manually set the origin via GCS or Lua script on every power cycle when flying indoors with non-GPS position sources."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-non-gps-navigation-landing-page.rst:46
#: 3dfa7cdad3a44fa999cb3ca109330999
msgid "**Typical setup for indoor flight with optical flow or external navigation:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-non-gps-navigation-landing-page.rst:48
#: f9606f06718d4075920577e922bfddc8
msgid "Enable :ref:`AHRS_OPTIONS<AHRS_OPTIONS>` bit 3 to auto-record the origin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-non-gps-navigation-landing-page.rst:49
#: b5c82c8d4cb94811ade04d0b31e4cbf3
msgid "Fly outdoors first (or manually set :ref:`AHRS_ORIGIN_LAT<AHRS_ORIGIN_LAT>`, :ref:`AHRS_ORIGIN_LON<AHRS_ORIGIN_LON>`, :ref:`AHRS_ORIGIN_ALT<AHRS_ORIGIN_ALT>`) to establish a valid origin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-non-gps-navigation-landing-page.rst:50
#: dc1bd21dd9cb4cfd8302a0be61c3357f
msgid "Enable :ref:`AHRS_OPTIONS<AHRS_OPTIONS>` bit 4 to auto-restore the origin for non-GPS flights"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-non-gps-navigation-landing-page.rst:51
#: d61d60d9eb1e4b6988554c5b2ddfaf13
msgid "On subsequent indoor flights, the origin will be automatically restored from the saved parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-non-gps-navigation-landing-page.rst:53
#: 36002e71ac9f49f7ab27fa11df3f2591
msgid "ArduSub enables bit 4 (UseRecordedOriginForNonGPS) by default since underwater vehicles typically operate without GPS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-non-gps-navigation-landing-page.rst:56
#: e89405a620264b5682e410cb0740999a
msgid "The low cost IMUs (accelerometers, gyros, compass) used in most autopilots drift too quickly to allow position estimation without an external velocity or position source.  In other words, low-cost IMUs on their own are not sufficient for estimating position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-non-gps-navigation-landing-page.rst:59
#: 24989b4bc6054ab3b259ea090c535ff5
msgid "A board with more than 1MB of flash is required to run non-GPS navigation, except for Vicon as 1MB boards still support the GPS_INPUT message, although they don't support the GLOBAL_VISION_POSITION_ESTIMATE so they have to be run using the GPS_INPUT message. See :ref:`Firmware Limitations <common-limited_firmware>` for details."
msgstr ""
